<title>ITALY: CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO RESULTS AND STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO RESULTS AND STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>VENAFRO, Italy 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in the</p>
<p>192-km first stage of the Tirreno-Adriatico cycle race from</p>
<p>Sorrento to Venafro on Thursday (Italians unless stated):</p>
<p>1. Endrio Leoni  four hours 47 minutes 54 seconds</p>
<p>2. Nicola Minali</p>
<p>3. Mario Traversoni</p>
<p>4. Jan Svorada (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>5. Fulvio Frigo</p>
<p>6. Erik Zabel (Germany)</p>
<p>7. Biagio Conte</p>
<p>8. Sergio Previtali</p>
<p>9. Claudio Camin</p>
<p>10.Sergei Outschakov (Ukraine) all same time as Leoni</p>
<p>Standings (including Wednesday's time trial):</p>
<p>1. Rolf Sorensen (Denmark) 4:52.31</p>
<p>2. Erik Dekker (Netherlands) two seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Gianluca Pianegonda same time</p>
<p>4. Maurizio Fondriest three seconds</p>
<p>5. Gabriele Colombo four seconds</p>
<p>6. Leon Van Bon (Netherlands) same time</p>
<p>7. Frank Corvers five seconds</p>
<p>8. Roberto Petito</p>
<p>9. Paolo Savoldelli same time</p>
<p>10.Michele Bartoli six seconds</p>
</text>
